    "title": "REQ-042: Reject telemetry samples with a timestamp too far in the future",
    "file": "requirements/REQ-042.md",
    "text": "# REQ-042: Reject telemetry samples with a timestamp too far in the future\n\nRequirement id: REQ-042\nComponent: src/telemetry/ingest.py\nPriority: Medium\n\n## Statement\n\nThe ingest service must reject any telemetry sample whose timestamp is more\nthan 24 hours after the current time. A rejected sample must not be stored.\nThe rejection reason must mention \"future\".\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A sample timestamped 25 hours in the future is rejected.\n2. A sample timestamped 23 hours in the future is accepted.\n3. The rejection reason contains the word \"future\".\n4. All existing tests keep passing.\n5. A new automated test covers criteria 1 to 3 and names REQ-042.\n\n## Notes for the implementer\n\n- validate_sample() already takes an injectable \"now\" for testing.\n- Do not change the public function names.\n",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-23T18:00:46+00:00"
  },
